lessons.concept:
▸  THE POINT
if lets a program choose. "If this is true, do that. Otherwise, do
something else."

▸  THE SHAPE
    if age >= 18 {
        fmt.Println("adult")
    } else {
        fmt.Println("child")
    }
Go checks the condition (age >= 18). If it is true, the first block
runs. If not, the else block runs. Never both.

▸  COMPARING
    ==   equal to            (two equals signs!)
    !=   not equal to
    <    less than           >    more than
    <=   less or equal       >=   more or equal
Each comparison gives true or false.

Remember: = puts a value in a box. == asks "are these equal?"

▸  MORE THAN TWO CHOICES
    if score >= 90 {
        ...
    } else if score >= 50 {
        ...
    } else {
        ...
    }
Go checks from the top and runs the FIRST block that is true.

▸  COMBINING
    &&   and  - both must be true:    age >= 13 && age <= 19
    ||   or   - at least one true:    day == "Fri" || day == "Sat"

▸  TRY IT
Change temp to 35, then to 5. Run each time and predict first.

