lessons.concept:
A variable is a named piece of memory that holds a value of one type. Declare one with var:

    var age int = 30      // name, type, initial value
    var name = "Ada"      // type inferred from the value (string)
    var score int         // no value: starts at the zero value, 0

You can declare several at once in a group:

    var (
        width  = 3
        height = 4
    )

Assign a new value with `=`. The type never changes: once age is an int, it can only hold ints. A variable declared inside a function must be used, or the program does not compile (unused variables are usually bugs).

