lessons.concept:
`if` runs a block only when a condition is true:

    if temp > 30 {
        fmt.Println("hot")
    } else if temp > 15 {
        fmt.Println("mild")
    } else {
        fmt.Println("cold")
    }

Rules: no parentheses around the condition, braces are always required, and the condition must be a bool (Go won't treat 0 or "" as false).

An if can start with a short statement, separated by a semicolon. Variables declared there exist only inside the if/else:

    if n := len(name); n > 5 {
        fmt.Println("long name:", n)
    }

