lessons.concept:
A variadic function takes any number of arguments of one type. Write `...` before the type of the last parameter. Inside the function that parameter is a slice:

    func sum(nums ...int) int {
        total := 0
        for _, n := range nums { total += n }
        return total
    }
    sum()          // 0
    sum(1, 2, 3)   // 6

fmt.Println is variadic, which is why it takes any number of values. To pass an existing slice, spread it with `...`:

    numbers := []int{4, 5, 6}
    sum(numbers...)

