lessons.concept:
▸  VALUE SWITCH
    switch day {
    case "sat", "sun":
        fmt.Println("weekend")
    default:
        fmt.Println("weekday")
    }
No break needed; several values per case; cases can be any expression.

▸  TAGLESS SWITCH (an if-else chain)
    switch {
    case t < 12: ...
    case t < 18: ...
    default: ...
    }

▸  INIT STATEMENT
    switch n := len(xs); { case n == 0: ...; case n > 100: ... }

▸  TYPE SWITCH (preview - see Interfaces)
    switch v := x.(type) {
    case int:    // v is an int here
    case string: // v is a string here
    }

