lessons.concept:
Two ways to let callers react to WHICH error happened:

▸  SENTINEL ERRORS - exported values
    var ErrNotFound = errors.New("not found")
    ...
    if errors.Is(err, store.ErrNotFound) { ... }
Simple; good when the caller only needs to know the kind of failure.
The standard library has many: io.EOF, fs.ErrNotExist, sql.ErrNoRows,
context.Canceled.

▸  CUSTOM ERROR TYPES - carry data
    type ValidationError struct { Field, Reason string }
    func (e *ValidationError) Error() string { ... }
Callers extract the details with errors.As.

▸  ADD AN Unwrap METHOD to make your type part of a chain:
    func (e *QueryError) Unwrap() error { return e.Err }

▸  errors.Join (Go 1.20)
Combine several errors into one (e.g. validating many fields); Is/As
search all of them:
    return errors.Join(err1, err2)

