lessons.concept:
Sometimes code must differ per operating system or per build (say, a
debug build). Go never switches code on and off INSIDE a function -
instead, whole FILES are included or excluded:

▸  FILENAME SUFFIXES (automatic)
    net_linux.go        only built when GOOS=linux
    asm_amd64.s         only for GOARCH=amd64
    db_windows_arm64.go both conditions
    x_test.go           only in 'go test'

▸  //go:build CONSTRAINTS (first line of the file, then a blank line)
    //go:build linux && !cgo
    //go:build debug                   // go build -tags debug
    //go:build go1.23                  // only with Go 1.23+

▸  THE PATTERN
Put the platform-specific half of a function in two files with the same
function signature:
    clipboard_darwin.go   func copyText(s string) error { ... pbcopy ... }
    clipboard_linux.go    func copyText(s string) error { ... xclip ... }
and call copyText from portable code.

▸  RUNTIME CHECKS
For small differences, a plain 'if runtime.GOOS == "windows"' is fine.

