lessons.concept:
Some features exist mostly for generated code and special cases. Know
them when you read them:

▸  LABELLED break / continue  (common and fine)
    outer:
    for ... {
        for ... {
            if bad { continue outer }
        }
    }

▸  goto  (rare)
Jumps to a label in the same function; can't jump over variable
declarations or into blocks. Generated parsers use it. defer has
replaced 'goto cleanup' style code in Go.

▸  fallthrough
Forces execution into the next switch case's body (without testing its
condition). Must be the last statement in a case.

▸  BLANK IDENTIFIERS IN DECLARATIONS
    var _ io.Writer = (*MyWriter)(nil)   // interface compliance check
    import _ "image/png"                  // import for side effects (init)

▸  CONVERSIONS BETWEEN NAMED TYPES
type Celsius float64 and type Fahrenheit float64 are different types;
converting Celsius(f) is allowed (same underlying type) but changes the
MEANING only if you also compute.

