▸  YOUR TASK
Build a tiny in-memory notes API with the Go 1.22 mux:

    POST   /notes        body {"text": "..."}  -> 201 {"id":N,"text":...}
                         empty text            -> 400 {"error":"text required"}
    GET    /notes/{id}   -> 200 the note, 404 {"error":"not found"}
    DELETE /notes/{id}   -> 204, or 404

Protect the map with a sync.Mutex (handlers run concurrently). Then
exercise it with httptest so the output matches YOUR TASK exactly.

▸  HINTS
    - type store struct { mu sync.Mutex; next int; notes map[int]Note }
    - A writeJSON(w, status, v) helper keeps handlers short.
    - strconv.Atoi(r.PathValue("id")); a bad id is a 404 too.
    - A 204 response has no body.

