lessons.concept:
Readable Go code aligns the 'happy path' down the left edge and
handles errors and special cases early with a return
(100 Go Mistakes #2):

    // nested: the important code drifts right
    func join(a, b string, max int) (string, error) {
        if a != "" {
            if b != "" {
                s := a + b
                if len(s) <= max { return s, nil } else { return "", errTooLong }
            } else { return "", errEmpty }
        } else { return "", errEmpty }
    }

    // guard clauses: each problem exits immediately
    func join(a, b string, max int) (string, error) {
        if a == "" || b == "" { return "", errEmpty }
        s := a + b
        if len(s) > max { return "", errTooLong }
        return s, nil
    }

▸  THE RULES OF THUMB
    - Return early; avoid else after a return.
    - Invert conditions so the normal case isn't indented.
    - Reading only the left edge should tell you what the function
      does when everything goes right.
    - Extract a helper when a block grows deep anyway.

